# Agenda de aulas

Alunos marcam aulas e o professor confirma.

Stack: Static site.

## Run it locally

### Prerequisites

- Node.js
- Git

### Step by step

1. Clone the repository and enter the folder:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/you/agenda-de-aulas.git
   cd agenda-de-aulas
   ```
2. Install the dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install
   ```
3. Copy the variables and fill in the values:
   ```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```
4. Run the site:
   ```bash
   npm run dev
   ```

### Environment variables

| Variable | What it is for | Where to get it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` | Final site address, used in links and SEO. Visible in the browser. | Example: `https://meusite.com.br` |

No secret value is kept in the repository: fill in secrets only in your .env.

## Folder structure

| Folder | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| `src/pages/` | Each file becomes a site page. |
| `src/components/` | Reusable pieces (header, footer, cards). |
| `src/content/` | Posts and text in Markdown. |
| `public/` | Images and files copied as-is. |
| `dist/` | Generated site to publish (not committed). |

